"""Second-person "you" detector (layer 0, MLP down-projection unit 210).

The unit responds to the word "you" when a text addresses the reader. It is strongest on a
capitalised "You" (about 4.5), which usually opens a sentence. Lowercase "you" is strong
when it is the subject of a clause (after a comma, "and", "so", "then", "that": about 2.5)
and weaker when it is an object after a verb (about 1.5). Capitalised "Your" gives a weak
signal, lowercase "your" a very weak one. The auxiliary that follows a "you" ("You are",
"you have", "you're") gives a moderate one. Second-person pronouns in other languages
(你, 您, Вы, あなた, Vous, Você, คุณ) give a moderate one. Everything else is near 0.
"""

READS = ()

YOU = {"you", "You"}
CLAUSE_BEFORE = {",", "and", "so", "then", "that"}
AUX_AFTER_YOU = {"are", "have", "'re", "’re", "need", "will"}
FOREIGN_YOU = {"你", "您", "Вы", "вы", "あなた", "Vous", "vous", "Você", "ณ"}


