short consonantal starts are positive; internal vowel and final-consonant
pieces are negative. The preceding token's accents and nasal/vowel ending
adjust these predictions. Thai nasals, tone/cancellation marks, the vowel
carrier อ and vowel sign ื have separate offsets.

